message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on reusable fabric Christmas crackers. Christmas crackers would normally fall under 9505.10 (Christmas festive articles). Subheading 9505.10.25 covers "Other" Christmas articles of other materials, and 9505.10.15 covers glass, 9505.10.20 covers wood, 9505.10.25 covers other materials. Textile Christmas articles, however, are classified under 9505.10.35 or 9505.10.40... Checking the structure: 9505.10.10 is nativity scenes, 9505.10.15 is glass articles, 9505.10.25 is other (non-textile), 9505.10.30 is Christmas tree skirts, 9505.10.35 is stockings, and 9505.10.40 is other textile articles.

I recall the actual HTS lines: 9505.10.10 Nativity scenes and figures; 9505.10.15 Glass articles; 9505.10.25 Other (articles of other materials); 9505.10.30 Of textile materials (stockings); 9505.10.35 Tree skirts; 9505.10.40 Other textile; 9505.10.50 Other. A cotton-encased cracker is not a stocking or skirt, so it falls under the other textile articles line. The textile-based classification yields 9505.10.4000 for "Other" textile articles, which I'm going with.

{"hts_code": "9505.10.4000", "reason": "Reusable cotton-fabric-covered Christmas crackers are festive articles for Christmas of textile materials under heading 9505, falling in the 'other' textile Christmas articles subheading."}
